Use io and string.

Define function find_text taking haystack as a pointer to TcString, needle as a pointer to TcString returning a whole number:
    Let hay length be length of haystack.
    Let needle length be length of needle.
    If needle length is 0, give back 0.
    If needle length is more than hay length, give back -1.
    Let offset start at 0 as an unsigned number.
    Repeat while offset + needle length is at most hay length:
        Let matched be true.
        For every i from 0 as an unsigned number to needle length - 1:
            If haystack.data[offset + i] isn't equal to needle.data[i]:
                Set matched to false.
        If matched is true:
            Give back offset as a whole number.
        Add 1 to offset.
    Give back -1.
Done.

Let first haystack be str_from_bytes(bytes_ptr("sadbutsad"), bytes_len("sadbutsad")).
Let first needle be str_from_bytes(bytes_ptr("sad"), bytes_len("sad")).
Let second haystack be str_from_bytes(bytes_ptr("leetcode"), bytes_len("leetcode")).
Let second needle be str_from_bytes(bytes_ptr("leeto"), bytes_len("leeto")).
Say find_text(address of first haystack, address of first needle).
Say find_text(address of second haystack, address of second needle).
str_free(address of first haystack).
str_free(address of first needle).
str_free(address of second haystack).
str_free(address of second needle).
Return 0.
